  "body": "**What's missing:** the GUI's part move/rotate command, `MoveModel` (`crates/app/src/commands/move_model.rs`), has no MCP tool. The `camcraft-mcp` skill lists it as remaining gap 1. Without it, an agent driving `camcraft-cli mcp` can't place an imported part: it can't lift a STEP whose origin sits mid-part so the part's bottom is at Z0, or stand a part up 90°. The workarounds don't cover it:\n- `set_wcs` moves the work offset, not the part, so the stock and fixtures stay where they were relative to the model.\n- `move_fixture` refuses a part: `'<name>' is not a fixture` (`MoveFixture::new`).\n\n**Neighbour that works:** `move_fixture { name, position, rotation? }` places a fixture through `MoveFixture`, one undo step (`crates/app/src/mcp/fixture_tools.rs`).\n\n**Done means:**\n- A `move_model { name, position: [x, y, z], rotation?: [x, y, z, w] }` tool runs `MoveModel::new` through `env.history`, so it is one undo step. An omitted rotation keeps the part's current one.\n- It returns the part's new placement and each stock that followed it (stock made from that model, or the stock of a one-part document, as `MoveModel` already moves).\n- `MoveModel`'s own refusals come back as tool errors, by name: a fixture, a work offset, the machine table, an unknown name, a non-finite position or a quaternion that doesn't normalize.\n- In-process JSON-RPC tests pin all three: a move with its following stock, undo and redo, and the refusals.\n\nLabels per AGENTS.md for an agent-filed issue: `enhancement`, `P2`, `area:ui`, `source:agent` (this account can't set labels).\n",
